# .ignore - ripgrep/search-tool exclusions for agent tooling
#
# NOT a .gitignore replacement: git tracking is governed by .gitignore.
# This file exists because repo-wide text search was drowning in machine noise
# (41k-line lockfile, vendored copies, generated output). Structural dirs are
# also excluded to make code search surgical.
#
# Keep in mind what an exclusion here HIDES from grep/search tooling:
#   - package-lock.json     - dependency diffs won't match text search
#   - init/, example/       - find generated copies via scripts/sync-engine.mjs,
#                             not text search (they are engine/ duplicates)
#   - docs/                 - edit docs directly; search them with -g '!none'
#                             tricks if needed or remove their line below
# Everything under an entry is excluded recursively.

# Dependency store
node_modules/

# Lockfile: 41k lines of registry hashes, zero signal for code search
package-lock.json

# Generated deploy targets (byte-identical copies of engine/ - single source
# of truth is engine/, regenerate via node scripts/sync-engine.mjs)
example/
init/

# Build output
dist/

# Docs site output (Jekyll build)
docs/_site/

# Test artifacts
coverage/
.vite/

# Binary/logo assets
horcrux/

# OS/editor noise (belt and braces; .gitignore already covers these)
.git/
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store
